# Dev server troubleshooting (Windows) — don't chase these as code bugs

Full detail lives in `AGENTS.md → "Local dev server troubleshooting (Windows)"`.
Read that section before spending time editing `vite.config.ts` or blaming a
recent change (e.g. the Lovable `mcpPlugin()`, edge-function CORS work) when
you hit either of these:

1. **`npm run dev` hangs at `[optimizer] scanning dependencies...` forever.**
   Cause: zombie `node.exe` processes from prior crashed/killed sessions
   contending for file locks. Fix: `taskkill /IM node.exe /F`, delete
   `node_modules/.vite`, restart. (Confirm with the user before killing all
   node processes system-wide.)

2. **A browser-automation tool times out navigating to `localhost`/
   `127.0.0.1`, with no request ever reaching the dev server log, even
   though external HTTPS sites load fine and `curl` to the same local URL
   works.** Cause: endpoint-security software on this machine intercepts
   IPv4 loopback traffic. Fix: use `http://[::1]:PORT` (IPv6 loopback)
   instead — it bypasses the interception.
